2. Use the existing IP core, realize the camera image reading and output
The specific operation process:
• Use the wizard to create a new project, the project name is Lab_11.

• Create a new resource file and name it Lab_11 (Design Resources).

• Add IP core rgb2dvi_0 (Note: This IP core is the driver IP core of HDMI, which can be found in the attachment package IP folder.
The input is 24 bit RGB image data, field line and data valid signals, synchronous data clock, and the output is HDMI clock line, data
line), as shown in Fig. 11-5.

Note: PLL must be selected here, otherwise the clock resource will not be enough and an error will be reported
• Add the frequency divider IP core clk_wiz_0, set the generation clock mode to PLL, turn off the locked output signal (reset, locked is
valid by default), set the reset to Active Low, and set the output clock to 100MHz and 200MHz respectively , as shown in Fig. 11-6.

• Add Driver_IIC_0, Driver_MIPI_0, OV5647_Init_0 IP cores, after adding, as shown in Fig. 11-7.

• In Lab_11, enter the following code:
//This is a camera case program that reads the camera data and displays the image on the display in real time via MINI HDMI.

`timescale 1ns / 1ps

module
Lab_1( input
i_clk, input
i_rst,
input i_clk_rx_data_n,
input i_clk_rx_data_p,
input [1:0]i_rx_data_n,
input [1:0]i_rx_data_p,
input i_data_n,
input i_data_p,
inout i_camera_iic_sda,
output o_camera_iic_scl,
output o_camera_gpio,
output TMDS_Tx_Clk_N,
output TMDS_Tx_Clk_P,
output [2:0]TMDS_Tx_Data_N,
output [2:0]TMDS_Tx_Data_P
);
//Clock signal
